351	90,765,515,1135	351. Papilionaceous corolla of Locust.	A Locust blossom seen from the front: the broad veined standard spread above, with the two wings and the curved keel clustered below it.
352	30,1250,635,1945	352. Its petals displayed: s, standard; w, w, wings; k, the keel laid open.	The five petals laid out separately: the large rounded standard, s, at the top, a clawed wing, w, on each side, and the two keel petals, k, below.
353	655,1425,865,1945	353. Legume of Pea, open.	A pea pod split open along its seam into two long valves, with a row of round peas attached along one edge and the calyx at the base.
354	885,1265,1095,1795 - 995,1680,1095,1795 - 885,1775,935,1800	354. Flower of False Indigo No. 2.	A side view of a False Indigo flower, the large standard curving up and back over the wings and keel, set in a short toothed calyx on its stalk.
355	990,1510,1250,1905 - 990,1510,1085,1600 - 990,1600,1032,1700	355. Same, with the petals removed.	The same flower with its petals removed: ten separate stamens and the style curving up out of the calyx.
356	1270,1570,1600,1935 - 1270,1570,1400,1700	356. Flower of Amorpha, enlarged.	An Amorpha flower enlarged: a gland-dotted calyx holding a single wrapped petal, the standard, with a brush of stamens protruding beside it.
357	1290,1245,1540,1640 - 1400,1592,1540,1640	357. Stamens and pistil of the same.	The stamens of Amorpha, their long filaments joined in a short ring at the base, with the style standing among them.
